by":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T20:26:57-07:00","id":1100686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1099878-backerkit-questions-from-an-international-friend#post1099878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey everyone, I have an International friend who has some questions about Backerkit in regards to C20 and the rewards.<br /> <br /> He purchased 3 items from the C:tD 20th anniversary edition. They got his order, but they said his card will be charged later. He was wandering when &quot;later&quot; was. His credit card needs to be activated for international use before it can be charged outside Brazil. But for security reasons he wouldn't like to let it activated for a long, indefinite amount of time.<br /> <br /> Anyone have any experience with this? He's just wondering how it usually takes before they charge the card..<br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks in advance if you can help!</div> </div> </div> </div>My experience with Backerkit is that it's completely independent of the kickstarter transaction. <br /> <br /> As in it's not going to happen *automatically*, when they get the backerkit set up they'll send out notices to let people know that it's up and that shipping can be paid for, and any additional items that can be purchased, and then collect card data *through* backerkit and process it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user